 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Every Christmas, a Swedish town builds a 13-meter straw goat.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.111
  },
  {
   "text": "Most years, it ends up as a giant flaming torch.",
   "s": 3.411,
   "e": 5.853
  },
  {
   "text": "The first one, in 1966, burned on New Year's Eve.",
   "s": 6.153,
   "e": 9.1
  },
  {
   "text": "So G\u00e4vle got serious: guards, fences, even webcams.",
   "s": 9.4,
   "e": 12.269
  },
  {
   "text": "But the goat kept burning.",
   "s": 12.569,
   "e": 13.625
  },
  {
   "text": "And it gets weirder: in 2001, an American tourist torched it.",
   "s": 13.925,
   "e": 17.288
  },
  {
   "text": "He thought it was a legal tradition. He got 18 days in jail.",
   "s": 17.588,
   "e": 20.633
  },
  {
   "text": "In 2005, people dressed as Santa and a gingerbread man shot it with a flaming arrow.",
   "s": 20.933,
   "e": 25.934
  },
  {
   "text": "So far, 43 goats have been burned or wrecked.",
   "s": 26.235,
   "e": 28.526
  },
  {
   "text": "So this Christmas, the town will build another goat.",
   "s": 28.826,
   "e": 30.816
  }
 ],
